      "content": "i get that, but isn't it also true that a lot of the criticism is just based on old-fashioned views that don't account for how much better kids do when they actually have options? like, isn't the \"public good\" argument sometimes just used as an excuse to protect broken systems that aren't working for anyone anymore?",
